        "conditions": "",
        "product": "C6H5OH",
        "productName": "phenol",
        "distractors": ["C6H5ONa", "C6H6", "C6H5NH2"],
        "reaction": "Dow process",
        "explanation": "The aryl chloride is unreactive, so drastic conditions are needed. The initial product is sodium phenoxide $\\ce{C6H5ONa}$, which is acidified to give phenol."
      },
